523 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (A person is esteemed valuable when they have something of value they add to others. Your Value describes everything you have, you are, or you do that solves problems for others, puts you in useful demand and attracts a reward towards you. It is any trait, skill, ability, personality, qualification or grace that you possess that is beneficial to others and can meet their felt needs. Value can be spiritual, physical, emotional, intellectual, academic, or financial. It includes character, material possessions, gifts, skills, anointing, grace, certifications, expertise and strength of character. Simply put, value describes what you have that you can exchange for profit. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [2]
>>
