530 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The widow in the scripture used the oil she had and it supernaturally multiplied. Value multiplies when you deploy it. She exited failure into success, when the man of God instructed her to go ahead and sell the multiplied oil. According to 2 Kings 4:7, Elisha said, "Now sell the olive oil and pay your debts, and you and your sons can live on what is left over." The prophet instructed her to sell the oil, meaning God is not against productivity, enterprise and profitability. Why did not God, in all his benevolence, instruct her to give the oil out for free to her hungry neighbours? )
/E (The widow in the scripture used the oil she had and it supernaturally multiplied. Value multiplies when you deploy it. She exited failure into success, when the man of God instructed her to go ahead and sell the multiplied oil. According to 2 Kings 4:7, Elisha said, "Now sell the olive oil and pay your debts, and you and your sons can live on what is left over." The prophet instructed her to sell the oil, meaning God is not against productivity, enterprise and profitability. Why did not God, in all his benevolence, instruct her to give the oil out for free to her hungry neighbours? )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [2]
