/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The principle of reward and profit is important especially in productivity and enterprise. You need your value to be adequately rewarded materially or intangibly so that you will have more input to reinvest into growth, expansion and perpetuation of the value. When a value is unrewarded, it will die out eventually to loss of the owner of the value and the unrewarding users. Consumers of value who are not willing to reward it are usually the first to move on to go and look elsewhere when the dispensing of the value dries out due to lack of adequate rewards to sustain and increase the source of the value. The concept of rewards is very important in value, productivity and enterprise because anything that is unrewarded will diminish and die out. Rewards are not just the benefit of productivity, they are the perpetrators and enhancers of it. )
