<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Faults in foundation may not be obvious to the observer as they are mostly hidden under the earth. However, a good builder will not compromise a fault in the foundation for anything. When there is a fault in the foundation of a building, no matter how hidden, it is only a matter of time for this fault to amplify and bring the entire building down. The taller a building rises, the more amplified the effect of a fault in the foundation is. Similarly, the more successful a person becomes, the more magnified flaws in the character becomes. Character flaw will eventually catch up and bring down success, no matter how long it takes. )
/E (Faults in foundation may not be obvious to the observer as they are mostly hidden under the earth. However, a good builder will not compromise a fault in the foundation for anything. When there is a fault in the foundation of a building, no matter how hidden, it is only a matter of time for this fault to amplify and bring the entire building down. The taller a building rises, the more amplified the effect of a fault in the foundation is. Similarly, the more successful a person becomes, the more magnified flaws in the character becomes. Character flaw will eventually catch up and bring down success, no matter how long it takes. )
