/T (Additionally, in the sport of weight lifting, athletes are not judged only by the weight they can lift but also by how long they can stably stand under that weight. It is very possible for one to lift a load but be unable to stand under it. It is also dangerous to lift a load one can not stand under because the weight may cause one to come crashing down and incur injuries due to the crushing effect of the pressure of the load. Strong character is the required stamina to stand under the weight of success. It is dangerous to succeed to a level that one has not developed the moral strength to stand stably at.  )
