626 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Reputation is an offshoot of character. The multi-billion industry of advertising and branding is all about building a reputation. However, it is known that great marketing of a substandard product is eventually damaging. Without good content, advertising will only reveal the flaws of the product to more people. The number one rule for advertising and marketing is to make sure you are good at what you do and the product will deliver on what it promises. Trying to build a reputation without character is building a mansion with a pack of cards. It will come crashing down. The best strategy to maintaining a great reputation is to consistently maintain a strong character. Character determines reputation. Reputation determines what comes to you which determines your level of success. It is good to have it at the back of your mind that everything you do and say contributes either to the building or destroying your character?)
