725 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Of course, it should be noted that a person can cross from a type of relationship to another. In fact, someone can occupy more than one type of relationship with you. However, this must be deliberately evaluated, assessed and consciously entered. You should allow people to cross from one type of relationship to another if you have discovered them suitable and consciously decided that they enter to that additional type of relationship. Therefore, for example, it is not impossible that work colleagues may eventually marry each other. However, this should be because they mutually discovered the desired quality of a suitable spouse in each other during the course of their work together, and not merely because the proximity of work influenced an emotional affiliation that they mistook that for a marital compatibility. Generally, roles, demands and personal attributes that make people effective as work partners are not necessarily be the ones that will be needed to complement each other as marriage partners. )
/E (Of course, it should be noted that a person can cross from a type of relationship to another. In fact, someone can occupy more than one type of relationship with you. However, this must be deliberately evaluated, assessed and consciously entered. You should allow people to cross from one type of relationship to another if you have discovered them suitable and consciously decided that they enter to that additional type of relationship. Therefore, for example, it is not impossible that work colleagues may eventually marry each other. However, this should be because they mutually discovered the desired quality of a suitable spouse in each other during the course of their work together, and not merely because the proximity of work influenced an emotional affiliation that they mistook that for a marital compatibility. Generally, roles, demands and personal attributes that make people effective as work partners are not necessarily be the ones that will be needed to complement each other as marriage partners. )
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [1]
>>
