/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (The foundation principle for all relationships is honour. Therefore, we must honour people at the same level with us. When we have people at the same level, we should be committed to their progress and support them. Let it be evident to your friends, partners and colleagues that you are not in competition with them but are committed to their success and you expect them to be committed to yours. As much as lies in your power, make them know they are your team-mates and not opponents.  )
/E (The foundation principle for all relationships is honour. Therefore, we must honour people at the same level with us. When we have people at the same level, we should be committed to their progress and support them. Let it be evident to your friends, partners and colleagues that you are not in competition with them but are committed to their success and you expect them to be committed to yours. As much as lies in your power, make them know they are your team-mates and not opponents.  )
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
736 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Down-line/Vertical Relationship: Everyone living a worthwhile life must have someone that they are raising. Down-lines include proteges, younger siblings, subordinates, juniors, children, employees etc. Remember, the foundational code for all relationships is honour. Therefore, the people under you equally deserve your honour. As a superior, the only authority you actually have over your down-lines is the honour they have for you. In other words, as a leader, the only right you have over people is their honour of you. If you lose that honour, you will see them walk away from you, then you will realise more than ever that their being under you was because of submission and honour out of volition. )
/E (Down-line/Vertical Relationship: Everyone living a worthwhile life must have someone that they are raising. Down-lines include proteges, younger siblings, subordinates, juniors, children, employees etc. Remember, the foundational code for all relationships is honour. Therefore, the people under you equally deserve your honour. As a superior, the only authority you actually have over your down-lines is the honour they have for you. In other words, as a leader, the only right you have over people is their honour of you. If you lose that honour, you will see them walk away from you, then you will realise more than ever that their being under you was because of submission and honour out of volition. )
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [1]
>>
