>>
endobj
781 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1009 0 R
/ActualText (Relationships are investments. The level of investiture of yourself into a relationship is what determines what you get out of it. Be careful not to waste your investments. Every beneficial relationship will make demands on you. There is no point seeking a relationship, you are not willing to give the demands it takes. So, do not seek or accept a level of relationship that you are not yet ready to meet up with the demands or commitments of that level. Having a level of relationship with a person is not compulsory. )
/Pg 68 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
782 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1010 0 R
/ActualText (Beneficial relationships must be intentionally pursued. There are people that are worth having in your life and will bring an advantage into your life. It is your responsibility to learn the laws that bring beneficial relationships to you. An example of such a law is shown in Prov. 18: 24; A man that hath friends must shew himself friendly: and there is a friend that sticketh closer than a brother .)
/Pg 68 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
783 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1011 0 R
/ActualText (Never forget that the average cross-section/survey your close and frequent relationships gives a good representation of who you are. The overview of the people around you is also a good prediction of your future. You can change your future by changing your associations/relationships. )
/Pg 68 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
784 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1012 0 R
/ActualText (Be henceforth be intentional in selecting and determining the relationships in and around your life. )
/Pg 68 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
